    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῐκελ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <u>Sicily</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			1.19
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.24
		</span></i>, etc.: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῐκελίδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, 
			Dor.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικελίδας</span>, name given by <i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			7.40
		</span></i>) to Asclepiades, and variously expld. in Sch.ad loc. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῑ-</span> in dactylics, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρχετε Σῑκελικαί . . </span>, <i><span class="en">
			Mosch.
			3.8
		</span></i>, etc.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σῑκελίδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.]</div>
